  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>:</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#8477;</mi></math> be a function defined by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mfenced><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, for some <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>,</p><p>Also given&nbsp;the range of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>,</p><p>Now we know that,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mfenced><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>(Assuming&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mfenced><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>k</mi></math>)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Now taking function&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></msqrt></msub><mfenced><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><msqrt><mi>m</mi></msqrt></msub><mfenced><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>m</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Now from equations <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></math>, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p>",
